Day 19 – HTML Forms & Web Security
🔹 What I Learned

HTML forms are the primary interface between users and servers and also the first attack surface of web applications.

🔹 Key Concepts

<form> – Data submission

<input> – User input fields

<textarea> – Long user inputs

<select> & <option> – Dropdown menus

🔹 Security Perspective

HTML forms are commonly exploited through:

SQL Injection

Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

CSRF

Credential harvesting

Parameter tampering

🔹 Key Takeaway

Understanding forms is essential to understanding how web attacks begin.
